  "onboardShowWords": "Show me the words again",
  "onboardFingerprintTitle": "Open it with your fingerprint?",
  "@onboardFingerprintTitle": {
    "description": "A QUESTION, and the screen is skippable with the skip at the same size as the button — ETHICAL-DESIGN.md forbids making the safe answer the hard one. There is a real reason to say no here: a fingerprint is easier to compel than a passphrase."
  },
  "onboardFingerprintBody": "So you do not have to type that passphrase every time.",
  "onboardFingerprintExplain": "Your passphrase is still the key. The fingerprint only opens this vault, only on this phone, and Android switches it off by itself if the fingerprints on the phone ever change — so nobody can add theirs and get in. It is never part of a backup.",
  "@onboardFingerprintExplain": {
    "description": "Four factual claims about scope. Deliberately the same promise the Settings row makes, word for word — two different descriptions of one security feature is how somebody ends up trusting neither."
  },
